\begin_layout Standard
This document provides guidelines on how to integrate CTU CAN FD into another HW design (e.g.
 SoC) on ASIC or FPGA.
 The SW integration is beyond the scope of this document.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To compile and integrate CTU CAN FD RTL in your system,
 do:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Clone CTU CAN FD GIT repository from 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "key-4"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Compile all files from 
\shape italic
src/slf_rtl.yml
\shape default
 to a VHDL library called ctu_can_fd_rtl.
 The files must be compiled in the order present in the 
\shape italic
src/slf_rtl.yml
\shape default
.
 This is typically done by TCL command like 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

read_vhdl
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 in ASIC or FPGA toolchains.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Instantiate and connect one of the following entities in your system:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
ctu_can_fd_top,
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
ctu_can_fd_top_avalon,
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
ctu_can_fd_top_ahb
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
ctu_can_fd_top_apb
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
See 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "chap:Signals-and-Generics"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "key-2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 for CTU CAN FD top level signals and parameters.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
