\begin_layout Section
Signals
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD has following logical interfaces:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Memory bus slave interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Interrupt
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Timestamp
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Scan control
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Test probe
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
CAN bus
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
Note Clock and reset signals are not mentioned here as they are described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "chap:Clocking-and-Reset"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Memory bus slave interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD has single 32-bit memory bus slave interface.
 This interface never stalls.
 CTU CAN FD can always consume the data provided or read the data requested within the next cycle.
 Therefore,
 the interface behaves like a RAM memory with byte-enable signals.
 There are following top-level wrappers for commonly known interfaces:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\shape italic
ctu_can_fd_top.vhd
\shape default
 - Default,
 RAM-like interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\shape italic
ctu_can_fd_top_avalon.vhd
\shape default
 - Altera Avalon interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\shape italic
ctu_can_fd_top_ahb.vhd
\shape default
 - AMBA High speed bus interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\shape italic
ctu_can_fd_top_apb.vhd
\shape default
 - AMBA Peripheral bus interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
Note APB,
 Avalon and RAM-like interfaces never stall.
 AHB interface stalls for one clock cycle on each read access.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For more details on memory bus interfaces (timing diagrams or signal namings) see 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "key-2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Interrupt
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD has single interrupt output.
 The interrupt output is named differently for each memory bus interface wrapper (
\color red
int
\color inherit
 or 
\color red
irq
\color inherit
).
 The interrupt is registered (therefore glitch-free).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Timestamp
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD can use external time-base to sample received frames,
 or do time-triggered transmission.
 The integrating system shall provide 64-bit upcounting binary counter on 
\color red
timestamp
\color inherit
 input to represent the time-base.
 If the integrator wants to use no time-base,
 they shall tie all bits of the 
\color red
timestamp
\color inherit
 input to high.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Scan control
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD supports scan-chain insertion.
 The 
\color red
scan_mode
\color inherit
 input is used to distinguish that device is in scan mode.
 See 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "chap:Design-for-Test"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

 for more details on design-for-test.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Test probe
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\color red
test_probe
\color inherit
 is a verification signal used only by CTU CAN FD testbench.
 This signal is present only on RAM-like interface wrapper.
 When integrating CTU CAN FD,
 you can leave this signal unconnected.
 In case you needed to synchronize to CAN bus timing,
 you can use fields of this signal for:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\color red
tx_trigger
\color inherit
 - Active for single clock cycle at start of SYNC segment of CAN bit.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\color red
rx_trigger_wbs
\color inherit
 - Active for single clock cycle at start of Sample point.
 Sample points of stuff bits are included.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\color red
rx_trigger_nbs
\color inherit
 - Active for single clock cycle at start of Sample point.
 Sample points of stuff bits are filtered.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These signals are synchronous to system clock,
 however there is no guarantee on timing.
 If you want to use them in your design,
 it is recommended to register them at the expense of one system clock cycle latency.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
CAN bus
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CTU CAN FD connects to the CAN bus by 
\color red
can_tx
\color inherit
 and 
\color red
can_rx
\color inherit
 signals.
 
\color red
can_rx
\color inherit
 is treated as asynchronous signal and resynchronized by CTU CAN FD (see more in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Signal-synchronizers"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

).
 
\color red
can_tx
\shape italic
\color inherit
 
\shape default
is synchronous to system clock,
 but it is not registered.
 When MODE and SETTINGS registers of CTU CAN FD are not changed at run-time,
 the 
\color red
can_tx
\color inherit
 is glitch free.
\end_layout

